<title>USA: Aero Systems says chief executive resigns.</title>
<headline>Aero Systems says chief executive resigns.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aero Systems Engineering Inc said its chief executive and president Roland Dilda resigned and was replaced by Leon Ring.</p>
<p>In a statement dated September 23, the company said Dilda left ASE to pursue other activities.  </p>
<p>Ring most recently served as a deputy project director of the National Wind Tunnel Complex. Ring was a senior vice president at ASE from 1993 to 1995, after serving as FluiDyne Engineering Corp's president when it was purchased by ASE.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
